# Generated by npm, not hand-edited
package-lock.json

# The API client, generated from the specification in @mmadel/openapi-spec by
# `npm run generate:api` (tickets T-85 and T-91). Its formatting is the
# generator's, not Prettier's, and the two disagree. Formatting it would make the committed files differ from what a
# regeneration produces, so a staleness check would report a stale client on
# a commit that changed nothing about the API. The generator owns these bytes.
/projects/api-client/src/generated

# Design and specification handoffs. They are exported artefacts rather than
# source - reformatting them produces a diff nobody can review against the
# document that was actually signed off, and the embedded images are single
# lines megabytes long.
/docs/**/*.html

# Tickets, for the same reason and one sharper one: Prettier RENUMBERS ordered
# lists. T-111 lists its acceptance criteria out of order deliberately - the ones
# checkable without a running backend first - and a reformat silently rewrote
# `5.` to `3.`, which left the ticket's own test table naming different criteria
# from the ones it now numbered. A ticket is a handed-over document; its bytes are
# the agreement.
/docs/tickets
